{
  "mn83:0.1": "Middle Discourses 83 ",
  "mn83:0.2": "About King Maghadeva ",
  "mn83:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn83:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Mithilā in the Maghadeva Mango Grove. ",
  "mn83:2.1": "Then the Buddha smiled at a certain spot. ",
  "mn83:2.2": "Then Venerable Ānanda thought, ",
  "mn83:2.3": "“What is the cause, what is the reason why the Buddha smiled? ",
  "mn83:2.4": "Realized Ones do not smile for no reason.” ",
  "mn83:2.5": "So Ānanda arranged his robe over one shoulder, raised his cupped palms toward the Buddha, and said, ",
  "mn83:2.6": "“What is the cause, what is the reason why the Buddha smiled? ",
  "mn83:2.7": "Realized Ones do not smile for no reason.” ",
  "mn83:3.1": "“Once upon a time, Ānanda, right here in Mithilā there was a just and principled king named Maghadeva, a great king who stood by his duty. ",
  "mn83:3.2": "He justly treated brahmins and householders, and people of town and country. ",
  "mn83:3.3": "And he observed the sabbath on the fourteenth, fifteenth, and eighth of the fortnight. ",
  "mn83:4.1": "Then, after many years, many hundred years, many thousand years had passed, King Maghadeva addressed his barber, ",
  "mn83:4.2": "‘My dear barber, when you see grey hairs growing on my head, please tell me.’ ",
  "mn83:4.3": "‘Yes, Your Majesty,’ replied the barber. ",
  "mn83:4.4": "When many thousand years had passed, the barber saw grey hairs growing on the king’s head. ",
  "mn83:4.5": "He said to the king, ",
